<title>UK: Railtrack shares up on technical bounce.</title>
<headline>Railtrack shares up on technical bounce.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Railtrack Plc jumped more than three percent on Wednesday, riding the crest of a sharp FTSE 100 rally and recovering from a sell-off over the last week, traders said.</p>
<p>By 0945 GMT, Railtrack shares were up 28p to 796-1/2p, near their record high of 807p hit on July 29.  </p>
<p>Its shares dropped six percent in the week to Tuesday, when they hit 758p.</p>
<p>Traders said they heard of no recommendation changes by analysts and no news to support the sharp share rally.</p>
<p>-- John Hanley, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
